ChangeLog
=========

wavelet-sharpen v0.2
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Ported to GIMP 3. GIMP 2.x is no longer supported, use v0.1.2 for it.
- Images of any precision are processed in floating point without loss, in
  the colour space of the image. Floating point images are not clipped.
- The script arguments keep their GIMP 2 names: amount, radius, luminance.
- GIMP's standard Reset, Load and Save Settings replace the reset button.
- The preview shows the alpha channel instead of full opacity.
- Fixed: building failed with GCC 10 and newer (multiple definitions).
- Fixed: reading outside of the image for selections smaller than 32 pixels.
- Fixed: the YCbCr conversion of "Sharpen luminance only" was not exactly
  reversible, which changed 16-bit and floating point images slightly.
- Indexed images, layer groups and layers with locked pixels are refused
  with an error message instead of being processed.
- Nothing is changed when the amount is 0.
- Added tests (tests/run.sh).
- Build system is now meson; translations are installed with the plugin.
- Added translations:
  - Dutch (thanks to Richard van der Luit)
  - Greek (thanks to Chris Sakalis)
- Fixed russian translation

wavelet-sharpen v0.1.2
